@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
+# Explicit decode bins and Hz model migration
+
+This companion patch targets the pending non-local-detector 0.7 API. Version 0.7
+has not been published or tagged by this patch. Publish the matching detector
+release before releasing this adapter. The separate compatibility-cap patch
+keeps the existing adapter below that breaking version until the coordinated
+rollout. The migrated adapter requires `non-local-detector>=0.7,<0.8` in both
+Python and conda dependency declarations.
+
+Recompute fitted models, decoded results, and derived analyses. Loading an old
+model for inspection does not establish new rate units or transition clocks.
+Refit from the original position/spike recording. GLM model persistence remains
+an unsupported upstream Patsy serialization path; this companion does not repair
+or qualify that path.
+
+PositionGroup keeps each source epoch's continuity in
+`position_info.attrs['valid_position_intervals']`, after clipping to the fetched
+recording. Original timestamps, training masks, environment labels, and encoding
+group labels remain on the tracking samples. NaN position rows remain present.
+Overlapping epochs or duplicate timestamps require an upstream ownership policy;
+the adapter rejects them instead of silently inferring continuity. An exact
+shared tracking-boundary sample anchors both physical interpolation endpoints.
+One indexed value cannot describe discontinuous positions or angles on opposite
+sides; use separate measured spans or sequence-local tracking for those epochs.
+This physical endpoint basis is separate from spike event ownership.
+
+The decoder constructs uniform bins at its configured `sampling_frequency`,
+independently of camera timestamps. Partial terminal bins are trimmed. A short interval between camera samples is
+decodable when its complete bins lie inside the measured interpolation support;
+it does not need a camera sample inside the interval. Bins are
+observed only when their entire span lies between finite measured samples of a
+declared tracking segment. Encoding's endpoint hold does not extend observed
+decode support. Explicit missing masks can be provided on the decode rows, or as
+a timestamped Series on the original tracking timeline using preceding-sample
+ownership. Missingness combines with measured support and never changes the
+identity of a requested interval.
+
+Each prediction interval starts a separate sequence. At a truly shared closing
+boundary, the earlier sequence excludes the boundary event; waveform marks use
+the same event mask. EM uses one uniform grid through masked gaps and therefore
+propagates its HMM instead of resetting. Result interval labels come from the
+actual requested bin spans, rather than from connected regions of missingness.
+Membership allows only endpoint roundoff (four ULP, capped at one percent of a
+bin width), so a shifted clock origin does not drop a complete bin or admit a
+materially partial bin. Interval masks stream one interval at a time to keep
+workspace proportional to the number of decode rows.
+
+Timestamped transition covariates can use the original tracking index or actual
+decode centers. Numeric covariates default to continuous interpolation; Boolean
+and non-numeric columns use preceding-sample categorical ownership. For numeric
+categories or angles, declare, for example:
+
+```python
+decoding_kwargs['discrete_transition_covariate_kinds'] = {
+    'route_id': 'categorical',
+    'heading': 'circular',  # radians, shortest-arc interpolation
+    'speed': 'continuous',
+}
+```
+
+Original covariates interpolate only within their finite tracking segments.
+Every transition row needs finite covariates, including rows where observations
+are masked. For gaps, supply explicit values on the actual decode-center index;
+the adapter raises instead of inventing covariates between epochs. Plain
+covariate dictionaries already need one value per requested decode bin. Fit
+transition tensors retain their original covariate axis when saved; prediction
+covariates are rebuilt for every requested interval.
+
+Ahead/behind analyses align actual position, heading, and track segment to saved
+result bin centers and bounds. They return one distance per result row, with NaN
+for missing or unsupported tracking. Categorical segment IDs use the preceding
+sample; angles follow the shortest arc. No raw camera-row zip is used.
+
+## Validation and remaining release gates
+
+`tests/decoding/test_time_grid_migration.py` executes the actual adapter method
+source and real detector without importing DataJoint table schemas. Its fixtures
+cover sorted and clusterless prediction/EM at 30 and 500 Hz tracking, missing
+tracking, epoch support preservation, shared event/mark ownership, nonstationary
+covariates, and perfect 500-bin trajectory decoding from 31 camera samples. It
+also writes and reads synthetic NWB tracking/spikes/marks/epochs before feeding
+those arrays to all four actual adapter paths. DataJoint is imported without
+opening a connection.
+
+Run the hermetic tests with a supported environment and the detector source
+checkout on PYTHONPATH:
+
+```sh
+PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
+NUMBA_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/spyglass-migration-numba \
+MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp/spyglass-migration-mpl \
+PYTHONPATH=/path/to/non_local_detector/src \
+uv run --no-sync python -m pytest --noconftest -o addopts= -o filterwarnings= \
+    tests/decoding/test_time_grid_migration.py -q
+```
+
+The review environment is Python 3.11.15, NumPy 2.4.6, SciPy 1.17.1, JAX 0.6.2,
+Pandas 2.3.3, Xarray 2026.4.0, DataJoint 0.14.9, and PyNWB 3.1.3. This satisfies
+the Python project declarations, but does not qualify the conda profile's
+`scipy<1.13` constraint. Before release, run the existing DataJoint/NWB pipeline
+suite with its normal database fixtures, verify model/result persistence for the
+selected supported backends, run the supported Python 3.10–3.12 matrix and conda
+profile, and compare representative scientific outputs after recomputation.
+The hermetic tests establish API and array/clock compatibility, not a complete
+production database qualification.
+
+This archived companion targets Spyglass commit
+`8d3cb4408ed5b86f28412c69434e8fa2af3b06aa`, whose adapter predates the later
+observed-acquisition changes. Its focused hermetic suite passed 27 cases. For the
+current observed-time adapter and its physical acquisition bridge, use the
+separately rebased current-state patch.
